oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome success
file Makefile kept 11
| # GNU Make sets `always_make_flag = always_make_set && (restarts == 0)` before
| # it brings the makefiles up to date and back to `always_make_set` afterwards
| # (main.c). Without the guard `-B` remakes `gen.mk` however current it is, the
| # remake moves its date, the read starts again, and it is remade again forever.
| # With it the makefile is remade once, the read goes around once, and the goals
| # are then built with `-B` still in force.
| all: ; @printf 'all restarts=[%s]\n' '$(MAKE_RESTARTS)' >> log
| include gen.mk
| gen.mk: gen.src
| 	@printf 'remade V=[%s]\n' '$(V)' >> log
| 	@cp gen.src gen.mk
file gen.mk touched 1
| V := from-gen
file gen.src kept 1
| V := from-gen
file log touched 2
| remade V=[from-gen]
| all restarts=[1]
